WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:30.758 --> 00:01:31.759
Blake.

3
00:01:33.261 --> 00:01:34.262
Blake.

4
00:01:35.513 --> 00:01:36.514
Sorry. Sarge.

5
00:01:37.139 --> 00:01:40.685
Pick a man. bring your kit.

6
00:01:40.768 --> 00:01:41.769
Yes. Sarge.

7
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:05.334
Don't dawdle.

8
00:02:05.835 --> 00:02:06.836
No. Sarge.

9
00:02:16.304 --> 00:02:17.596
Did they feed us?

10
00:02:18.431 --> 00:02:19.974
No. Just mail.

11
00:02:41.287 --> 00:02:42.705
Myrtle's having puppies.

12
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:46.876
You get anything?

13
00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.586
No.

14
00:02:50.254 --> 00:02:52.173
I'm bloody starvin'. aren't you?

15
00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:55.676
Thought we might get
some decent grub out here.

16
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:59.055
It was the only reason
I decided against the priesthood.

17
00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:06.228
What you got there?

18
00:03:06.312 --> 00:03:07.313
Ham and bread.

19
00:03:08.022 --> 00:03:09.231
Where did you find that?

20
00:03:10.149 --> 00:03:11.442
I have my uses.

21
00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:14.570
Here.

22
00:03:20.201 --> 00:03:21.660
Tastes like old shoe.

23
00:03:22.453 --> 00:03:25.456
Cheer up. This time next week.
it'll be chicken dinner.

24
00:03:26.791 --> 00:03:27.792
Not me.

25
00:03:29.085 --> 00:03:30.336
My leave got canceled.

26
00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:32.254
They say why?

27
00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:34.423
No idea.

28
00:03:36.175 --> 00:03:37.885
It's easier not to go back at all.

29
00:03:41.514 --> 00:03:42.515
Coming through!

30
00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:51.774
Something's up. Did you hear anything?

31
00:03:52.316 --> 00:03:53.317
No.

32
00:03:54.485 --> 00:03:55.778
Has to be the push. right?

33
00:03:57.696 --> 00:03:59.698
Ten bob says we're going up.

34
00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:01.742
I'm not taking that bet.

35
00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:04.412
Why? 'Cause you know I'm right?

36
00:04:04.495 --> 00:04:07.373
No. because you haven't got ten bob.

37
00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:12.711
In your own time. gentlemen.

38
00:04:13.796 --> 00:04:16.257
- Is there any news. Sarge?
- News of what?

39
00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.843
The big push.
It was supposed to happen weeks ago.

40
00:04:18.926 --> 00:04:20.553
They told us we'd be home by Christmas.

41
00:04:20.636 --> 00:04:22.930
Yes. well. sorry to disrupt
your crowded schedule. Blake.

42
00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:25.349
but the brass hats
didn't fancy it in the snow.

43
00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:27.810
More's the pity. Sarge.
I could've done with some turkey.

44
00:04:27.893 --> 00:04:30.855
Well. I'll make sure to relay
your displeasure to command.

45
00:04:30.938 --> 00:04:32.815
So. what's on the cards then.
Sergeant?

46
00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:34.608
The Hun are up to something.

47
00:04:34.692 --> 00:04:35.734
Any idea what?

48
00:04:35.818 --> 00:04:38.529
No. But it's about to ruin our weekend.

49
00:04:45.995 --> 00:04:47.329
Now. listen.

50
00:04:47.413 --> 00:04:49.748
Erinmore is inside. so tidy yourselves up.

51
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.462
Never know. might be mentions
in dispatches for this one...

52
00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.756
if you don't bugger it up.

53
00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.220
Must be something big
if the general's here.

54
00:05:13.481 --> 00:05:15.733
Lance Corporals
Blake and Schofield. sir.

55
00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:20.112
Which one of you is Blake?

56
00:05:20.196 --> 00:05:21.197
Sir.

57
00:05:21.864 --> 00:05:24.533
You have a brother.
a lieutenant in the 2nd Devons?

58
00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:27.328
Yes. sir. Joseph Blake. Is he...

59
00:05:27.411 --> 00:05:29.205
Alive. As far as I know.

60
00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:32.750
And with your help.
I'd like to keep it that way.

61
00:05:33.584 --> 00:05:36.045
Sanders tells me
you're good with maps. That true?

62
00:05:36.795 --> 00:05:37.796
Good enough. sir.

63
00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.090
So...

64
00:05:42.092 --> 00:05:44.011
we are here.

65
00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:47.890
The 2nd Devons are advancing here.

66
00:05:48.474 --> 00:05:50.351
How long will it take you to get there?

67
00:05:51.852 --> 00:05:53.354
I don't understand. sir.

68
00:05:53.437 --> 00:05:56.232
- Sir. that land is held by the Germans.
- Germans have gone.

69
00:05:57.608 --> 00:05:59.401
Don't get your hopes up.

70
00:05:59.485 --> 00:06:01.987
It appears to be a strategic withdrawal.

71
00:06:03.155 --> 00:06:07.034
They seem to have created a new line.
nine miles back here by the looks of it.

72
00:06:07.618 --> 00:06:09.912
Colonel Mackenzie
is in command of the 2nd.

73
00:06:10.871 --> 00:06:14.583
He sent word yesterday morning
he was going after the retreating Germans.

74
00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:17.878
He is convinced he has them on the run.

75
00:06:17.962 --> 00:06:20.923
that if he can break their lines now.
he will turn the tide.

76
00:06:22.383 --> 00:06:23.384
He is wrong.

77
00:06:24.093 --> 00:06:28.639
Colonel Mackenzie has not seen
these aerials of the enemy's new line.

78
00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:30.140
Come around here. gentlemen.

79
00:06:32.393 --> 00:06:35.479
Three miles deep.
field fortifications. defenses.

80
00:06:35.563 --> 00:06:38.148
artillery the like of which
we've never seen before.

81
00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:42.653
The 2nd are due to attack the line
shortly after dawn tomorrow.

82
00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:45.239
They have no idea
what they're in for.

83
00:06:46.073 --> 00:06:47.324
And we can't warn them.

84
00:06:47.408 --> 00:06:50.411
As a parting gift.
the enemy cut all our telephone lines.

85
00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.498
Your orders are to get to the 2nd
at Croisilles Wood.

86
00:06:54.582 --> 00:06:57.126
one mile southeast
of the town of Écoust.

87
00:06:58.043 --> 00:07:00.004
Deliver this to Colonel Mackenzie.

88
00:07:00.087 --> 00:07:03.007
It is a direct order
to call off tomorrow morning's attack.

89
00:07:03.674 --> 00:07:05.759
If you don't.
it will be a massacre.

90
00:07:06.552 --> 00:07:10.431
We will lose two battalions.
1.600 men. your brother among them.

91
00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.892
Do you think
you can get there in time?

92
00:07:13.976 --> 00:07:15.060
Yes. sir.

93
00:07:15.144 --> 00:07:16.520
Any questions?

94
00:07:16.604 --> 00:07:18.063
- No. sir.
- Good.

95
00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.690
Over to you. Lieutenant.

96
00:07:22.735 --> 00:07:24.111
Supplies. gentlemen.

97
00:07:25.571 --> 00:07:29.658
Map. torches. grenades.
and a couple of little treats.

98
00:07:30.868 --> 00:07:33.829
Leave immediately. Take this trench west
up on Sauchiehall Street.

99
00:07:33.912 --> 00:07:36.165
Then northwest on Paradise Alley
at the front.

100
00:07:36.248 --> 00:07:39.084
Continue along the front line
until you find the Yorks.

101
00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:40.711
Give this note to Major Stevenson.

102
00:07:40.794 --> 00:07:43.464
He's holding the line
at the shortest span of no-man's-land.

103
00:07:43.547 --> 00:07:44.882
You'll cross there.

104
00:07:45.466 --> 00:07:47.384
It'll be daylight. sir.
They'll see us.

105
00:07:47.468 --> 00:07:49.219
There's no need to be concerned.

106
00:07:49.303 --> 00:07:50.971
You should meet no resistance.

107
00:07:57.061 --> 00:07:59.605
Sir. is... is it just us?

108
00:08:00.564 --> 00:08:05.027
"Down to Gehenna or up to the Throne.
He travels the fastest who travels alone."

109
00:08:05.986 --> 00:08:08.572
- Wouldn't you say. Lieutenant?
- Yes. sir. I would.

110
00:08:11.116 --> 00:08:12.117
Good luck.

111
00:08:22.461 --> 00:08:24.672
Blake. let's talk about this
for a minute.

112
00:08:24.755 --> 00:08:25.756
Why?

113
00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.431
Blake!

114
00:08:41.814 --> 00:08:43.190
We just need to think about it.

115
00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:45.484
There's nothing to think about.
It's my big brother.

116
00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:48.987
- We should at least wait until it's dark.
- Erinmore said to leave immediately.

117
00:08:49.071 --> 00:08:51.115
Erinmore's
never seen no-man's-land.

118
00:08:51.198 --> 00:08:52.783
We won't make it ten yards.

119
00:08:52.866 --> 00:08:53.784
If we just wait...

120
00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:56.453
You heard him.
He said the Boche have gone.

121
00:08:56.995 --> 00:08:58.997
Is that why he gave us grenades?

122
00:09:10.134 --> 00:09:12.177
- Watch where you're going.
- Sorry.

123
00:09:21.395 --> 00:09:23.397
All I'm saying is that we wait.

124
00:09:23.856 --> 00:09:26.859
Yes. you would say that
'cause it's not your brother. is it?

125
00:09:29.653 --> 00:09:33.282
Look. the last time I was told
the Germans were gone. it didn't end well.

126
00:09:34.241 --> 00:09:36.285
You don't know. Blake.
You weren't there.

127
00:09:39.121 --> 00:09:40.914
Excuse me. Excuse me.

128
00:09:40.998 --> 00:09:43.000
Excuse me.

129
00:09:47.337 --> 00:09:49.423
You're going up the down trench.
you bloody idiot.

130
00:09:49.506 --> 00:09:50.883
Orders of the general. sir.

131
00:10:03.854 --> 00:10:05.939
All right.
say the Boche have gone.

132
00:10:06.607 --> 00:10:08.692
Nine miles would take us.
what. six hours?

133
00:10:08.776 --> 00:10:10.277
Eight at the very most.

134
00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.404
So. we've got time to wait
until the sun sets.

135
00:10:12.488 --> 00:10:13.822
- It's enemy territory.
- Otherwise we'll be wide open.

136
00:10:13.906 --> 00:10:15.532
We've got no idea what we're walking into.

137
00:10:15.616 --> 00:10:19.745
Blake. if we're not clever about this.
no one will get to your brother.

138
00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:21.830
I will.

139
00:10:24.416 --> 00:10:26.627
We're here. This is the front line.

140
00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:30.839
Now we need to find the Yorks.

141
00:11:16.051 --> 00:11:17.594
Sorry. mate.

142
00:11:18.178 --> 00:11:20.222
- Watch who you're shoving.
- Get out of the way.

143
00:11:20.305 --> 00:11:22.474
Who the fuck do you think you are.
pushing wounded soldiers?

144
00:11:22.558 --> 00:11:23.934
I didn't know. Let go of me!

145
00:11:24.017 --> 00:11:26.520
Arsehole knocked down our sergeant.
The man's fucking wounded!

146
00:11:26.603 --> 00:11:28.689
All right. I'm sorry.
All right? I'm sorry!

147
00:11:28.772 --> 00:11:29.982
- We're on commission.
- Just let me through.

148
00:11:30.065 --> 00:11:32.109
- Orders from the general.
- Just let me through.

149
00:11:33.443 --> 00:11:34.444
Get out of the way.

150
00:11:36.238 --> 00:11:38.657
All right.
Just watch where you're going.

151
00:12:08.478 --> 00:12:09.479
It's bloody quiet.

152
00:12:10.898 --> 00:12:12.566
Was it like this before Thiepval?

153
00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.401
Don't remember.

154
00:12:15.402 --> 00:12:16.862
You don't remember the Somme?

155
00:12:17.362 --> 00:12:19.656
- Not really.
- Hey. mind us. Come on.

156
00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:23.827
Well. you did all right out of it.

157
00:12:24.786 --> 00:12:26.121
At least wear your ribbon.

158
00:12:27.205 --> 00:12:28.540
Don't have it anymore.

159
00:12:29.541 --> 00:12:32.044
What? You lost your medal?

160
00:12:32.127 --> 00:12:33.337
Heads down. boys.

161
00:12:34.838 --> 00:12:36.924
Come on. lads. Keep digging.

162
00:12:41.053 --> 00:12:42.054
Stay low.

163
00:12:49.269 --> 00:12:50.854
For God's sake. careful there.

164
00:12:50.938 --> 00:12:52.564
You're stepping on the dead.

165
00:12:52.648 --> 00:12:53.732
That's our sergeant.

166
00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:56.777
Be better washing them out of this dugout
with a bloody hose.

167
00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.487
Do you know where the Yorks are?

168
00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.031
The next bend.
you'll be standing on top of half of them.

169
00:13:01.114 --> 00:13:02.532
Shot to hell two nights ago.

170
00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:13.251
Yorks?

171
00:13:13.669 --> 00:13:14.753
Yes. Corp.

172
00:13:14.836 --> 00:13:16.046
Where's Major Stevenson?

173
00:13:16.588 --> 00:13:18.924
Was killed.
Couple of nights ago. Corporal.

174
00:13:19.591 --> 00:13:21.134
Lieutenant Leslie has command.

175
00:13:21.677 --> 00:13:22.803
Where can we find him?

176
00:13:23.553 --> 00:13:24.596
Next dugout.

177
00:13:32.771 --> 00:13:33.772
Here.

178
00:13:38.986 --> 00:13:39.987
Sir?

179
00:13:40.654 --> 00:13:42.781
- Lieutenant Leslie. sir?
- What is it?

180
00:13:42.864 --> 00:13:44.741
We have a message
from General Erinmore.

181
00:13:44.825 --> 00:13:46.535
- Are you our relief?
- No. sir.

182
00:13:46.618 --> 00:13:48.537
Then when the fucking hell are they due?

183
00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:51.164
We don't know. sir.
but we've got orders to cross here.

184
00:13:51.248 --> 00:13:53.041
That is the German front line.

185
00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:54.126
We know. sir.

186
00:13:54.584 --> 00:13:56.169
If you'll just take the letter.

187
00:13:58.422 --> 00:13:59.965
Settle a bet. What day is it?

188
00:14:01.174 --> 00:14:02.217
Friday.

189
00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.052
Friday? Well. none of us was right.

190
00:14:04.136 --> 00:14:06.847
- This idiot thought it was Tuesday.
- Sorry. sir.

191
00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.851
Are they out of their fucking minds?

192
00:14:10.934 --> 00:14:13.937
One slow night. the brass think
the Hun have just gone home?

193
00:14:14.021 --> 00:14:15.647
Do you think they're wrong. sir?

194
00:14:16.815 --> 00:14:19.276
We lost an officer and three men
two nights ago.

195
00:14:19.359 --> 00:14:21.028
They were shot to bits patching up wire.

196
00:14:21.111 --> 00:14:23.947
We dragged two of them back here.
Needn't have bothered...

197
00:14:24.031 --> 00:14:27.159
Sir. the general is sure
the enemy have withdrawn.

198
00:14:27.242 --> 00:14:29.244
- There are aerials of the new line...
- Shut up.

199
00:14:29.327 --> 00:14:31.830
We fought and died
over every inch of this fucking place.

200
00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:34.291
Now they suddenly give us miles.
It's a trap.

201
00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.338
But chin up.
There's a medal in it. for sure.

202
00:14:40.422 --> 00:14:43.175
Nothing like a scrap of ribbon
to cheer up a widow.

203
00:14:45.927 --> 00:14:47.345
All right.

204
00:14:50.182 --> 00:14:51.850
Where's the nearest way through. sir?

205
00:14:51.933 --> 00:14:54.811
Our wire's a mess.
but there is a path through of sorts.

206
00:14:54.895 --> 00:14:56.855
Rushworth. let him look.

207
00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.987
Straight ahead to the left.
past the dead horses.

208
00:15:04.071 --> 00:15:05.781
There's a gap directly behind them.

209
00:15:06.782 --> 00:15:09.826
Useful because if it's dark.
you follow the stench.

210
00:15:09.910 --> 00:15:13.705
When you get to the second wire.
look out for the bowing chap.

211
00:15:13.789 --> 00:15:15.665
There's a small break just beside him.

212
00:15:15.749 --> 00:15:18.460
The German line
is 150-odd yards after that.

213
00:15:19.127 --> 00:15:21.922
Watch out for the craters.
They're deeper than they look.

214
00:15:22.005 --> 00:15:23.799
If you fall in. there's no getting out.

215
00:15:24.341 --> 00:15:25.342
This way.

216
00:15:27.385 --> 00:15:28.386
Wake up. Kilgour.

217
00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:30.305
Bloody waste of space.

218
00:15:30.388 --> 00:15:32.307
Any cover. sir?
Anywhere to jump off from?

219
00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:34.559
No. The sap trench
was blown to hell weeks ago.

220
00:15:34.643 --> 00:15:36.061
It was full of bodies. anyway.

221
00:15:36.144 --> 00:15:38.063
Your best bet is to pop over here.

222
00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.444
If you do get shot.
try to make it back to the wire.

223
00:15:44.528 --> 00:15:46.530
We won't come after you.
not till it's dark.

224
00:15:46.613 --> 00:15:50.742
And if by some fucking miracle
you do make it. send up a flare.

225
00:15:50.826 --> 00:15:51.952
Don't have any. sir.

226
00:15:52.828 --> 00:15:55.205
Well. get him one. Kilgour.
Make yourself useful.

227
00:15:55.288 --> 00:15:56.289
Yes. sir.

228
00:15:59.501 --> 00:16:02.754
Through this holy unction.
may the Lord pardon you your faults

229
00:16:02.838 --> 00:16:04.673
and whatever sins
thou has committed.

230
00:16:08.051 --> 00:16:10.011
I do hate losing these to the Hun.

231
00:16:10.095 --> 00:16:14.599
So. when they start shooting at you.
could you be so kind as to throw it back.

232
00:16:14.683 --> 00:16:15.767
There's a good chap.

233
00:16:19.104 --> 00:16:20.105
Cheerio.

234
00:16:27.988 --> 00:16:28.989
You sure?

235
00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:31.616
Yes.

236
00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:38.915
Age before beauty.

237
00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:27.941
You all right?

238
00:18:30.735 --> 00:18:31.736
Look for cover.

239
00:18:53.967 --> 00:18:54.968
Sap trench.

240
00:20:22.931 --> 00:20:23.932
Stay still.

241
00:20:32.941 --> 00:20:34.150
They're ours.

242
00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:37.695
Keep going.
We're halfway.

243
00:21:42.677 --> 00:21:44.679
There's a gap. In the wire.

244
00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:43.988
Sco.

245
00:23:08.096 --> 00:23:09.764
There. That's the front line.

246
00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:36.749
Fuck me.

247
00:23:37.625 --> 00:23:39.002
They really have gone.

248
00:24:00.273 --> 00:24:01.482
Your hand all right?

249
00:24:03.151 --> 00:24:04.861
Put it through an effing German.

250
00:24:06.696 --> 00:24:07.739
Patch it up.

251
00:24:08.323 --> 00:24:10.158
You'll be wanking again in no time.

252
00:24:11.701 --> 00:24:12.702
Wrong hand.

253
00:24:43.483 --> 00:24:44.609
They're not long gone.

254
00:25:08.508 --> 00:25:09.509
No good.

255
00:25:32.031 --> 00:25:33.032
Blocked.

256
00:25:34.075 --> 00:25:35.493
This might be a way through.

257
00:25:51.384 --> 00:25:52.593
Jesus.

258
00:26:01.060 --> 00:26:02.311
Look at this.

259
00:26:03.813 --> 00:26:05.022
It's massive.

260
00:26:08.109 --> 00:26:09.694
They built all this.

261
00:26:56.449 --> 00:26:57.825
Here's our way through.

262
00:26:58.367 --> 00:26:59.368
Sco.

263
00:27:01.245 --> 00:27:02.246
How 'bout this?

264
00:27:07.043 --> 00:27:08.294
Bloody hell.

265
00:27:11.380 --> 00:27:13.382
Even their rats are bigger than ours.

266
00:27:20.598 --> 00:27:22.225
What do you think's in the bags?

267
00:27:23.392 --> 00:27:24.977
You cannot be that hungry.

268
00:27:31.484 --> 00:27:34.278
Look at him.
Cocky little bastard.

269
00:27:35.404 --> 00:27:37.156
You could eat this. though.

270
00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:38.491
What is it?

271
00:27:38.574 --> 00:27:39.742
Boche dog meat.

272
00:27:41.911 --> 00:27:43.246
What's in the other boxes?

273
00:27:45.623 --> 00:27:47.667
- What's wrong?
- Trip wire.

274
00:27:48.793 --> 00:27:49.877
Don't move.

275
00:27:50.920 --> 00:27:52.129
Where is it?

276
00:27:54.674 --> 00:27:56.300
Goes from here to the door.

277
00:27:59.178 --> 00:28:01.556
- Jesus!
- No!

278
00:28:11.065 --> 00:28:12.984
Sco!

279
00:28:19.615 --> 00:28:21.534
Sco?

280
00:28:24.912 --> 00:28:25.913
Sco!

281
00:28:29.250 --> 00:28:31.878
Sco! Sco.

282
00:28:37.884 --> 00:28:38.885
Sco!

283
00:28:43.347 --> 00:28:45.266
Sco. Sco?

284
00:28:45.975 --> 00:28:48.311
Wake up. Wake up!

285
00:28:51.188 --> 00:28:52.607
Sco! Sco!

286
00:28:55.484 --> 00:28:57.737
Stand up! Stand up!

287
00:28:57.820 --> 00:28:59.572
Come on. Stand up!

288
00:29:00.364 --> 00:29:02.074
Up! Up! Up!

289
00:29:03.367 --> 00:29:04.368
Come on!

290
00:29:04.952 --> 00:29:05.953
Stand up!

291
00:29:10.666 --> 00:29:12.209
The whole thing's coming down.

292
00:29:18.633 --> 00:29:20.343
You keep hold of me!

293
00:29:33.856 --> 00:29:35.608
We need to keep moving.

294
00:29:35.691 --> 00:29:37.026
Come on!

295
00:29:37.109 --> 00:29:39.070
I can't see. I can't see!

296
00:29:40.655 --> 00:29:42.823
Stop! Stop. stop. stop. stop! Stop!

297
00:29:43.616 --> 00:29:44.909
It's a mine shaft.

298
00:29:45.952 --> 00:29:47.286
We'll have to jump.

299
00:29:47.995 --> 00:29:49.205
All right. come on.

300
00:29:52.166 --> 00:29:54.543
You're going to have to jump.
Just jump.

301
00:29:54.627 --> 00:29:57.588
- I can't. I can't see!
- You need to trust me.

302
00:29:57.672 --> 00:29:58.673
Jump!

303
00:30:05.596 --> 00:30:08.140
Don't let go of me! Don't let go!

304
00:30:11.686 --> 00:30:13.396
Light! There's light.

305
00:30:25.491 --> 00:30:28.119
Stop. stop.

306
00:30:28.202 --> 00:30:29.537
Just let me stand.

307
00:30:33.124 --> 00:30:34.625
Dirty bastards!

308
00:30:40.464 --> 00:30:43.592
Careful. They may have left other traps.

309
00:30:52.435 --> 00:30:53.769
Jesus.

310
00:31:04.572 --> 00:31:07.533
Dust.
So much dust in my eyes.

311
00:31:16.792 --> 00:31:18.335
Here.

312
00:31:18.419 --> 00:31:19.712
Have some of mine.

313
00:31:25.926 --> 00:31:27.845
I wish I'd shot that rat now.

314
00:31:29.055 --> 00:31:31.348
I wish you'd picked
some other bloody idiot.

315
00:31:31.974 --> 00:31:34.852
- What?
- Why in God's name did you choose me?

316
00:31:35.811 --> 00:31:39.148
- I didn't know what I was picking you for.
- No. you didn't.

317
00:31:39.231 --> 00:31:41.650
You never know.
That's your problem.

318
00:31:45.196 --> 00:31:46.405
All right. then go back.

319
00:31:47.865 --> 00:31:50.493
Nothing's stopping you. You can go
all the way bloody home if you want.

320
00:31:50.576 --> 00:31:51.577
Don't.

321
00:31:51.660 --> 00:31:52.787
Just don't.

322
00:31:54.789 --> 00:31:56.874
I didn't know what I was picking you for.

323
00:31:57.583 --> 00:32:01.087
I thought they were going to send us
back up the line or for food or something.

324
00:32:02.129 --> 00:32:05.424
I thought it was going to be
something easy. All right?

325
00:32:07.301 --> 00:32:08.969
I never thought it would be this.

326
00:32:15.935 --> 00:32:17.561
So. do you want to go back?

327
00:32:21.732 --> 00:32:23.359
Just fire the fucking flare.

328
00:32:38.958 --> 00:32:40.501
Up yours. Lieutenant.

329
00:32:56.350 --> 00:32:57.643
Do you know where we are?

330
00:32:59.478 --> 00:33:02.898
Écoust is directly southeast.

331
00:33:04.608 --> 00:33:06.152
And if we keep that bearing...

332
00:33:07.403 --> 00:33:08.696
we should make it.

333
00:33:12.658 --> 00:33:13.659
Come on. then.

334
00:33:38.684 --> 00:33:39.727
Look at that.

335
00:33:40.603 --> 00:33:42.146
They destroyed their own guns.

336
00:33:43.480 --> 00:33:45.441
They destroyed their own trenches. too.

337
00:33:46.942 --> 00:33:48.611
What do you mean?

338
00:33:48.694 --> 00:33:51.155
Think they wanted us to go that way.

339
00:33:51.238 --> 00:33:52.865
They wanted to bury us.

340
00:34:00.247 --> 00:34:02.124
You bastard rats.

341
00:34:09.465 --> 00:34:13.260
Hey. did you hear that story
about Wilko?

342
00:34:13.344 --> 00:34:15.679
- How he lost his ear?
- I'm not in the mood.

343
00:34:16.263 --> 00:34:18.849
Keep your eyes on the trees.
Top of the ridge.

344
00:34:22.561 --> 00:34:24.146
Bet he told you it was shrapnel.

345
00:34:25.814 --> 00:34:27.566
What was it. then?

346
00:34:28.651 --> 00:34:32.029
Well. you know
his girl's a hairdresser. right?

347
00:34:32.863 --> 00:34:36.700
And he was moaning about the lack of
bathing facilities when he wrote to her.

348
00:34:37.493 --> 00:34:39.536
You remember
those rancid jakes at Arras?

349
00:34:39.620 --> 00:34:40.537
Yeah.

350
00:34:40.621 --> 00:34:43.666
Anyway. she sends him over this hair oil.

351
00:34:45.125 --> 00:34:48.212
Smells sweet. Like Golden Syrup.

352
00:34:50.256 --> 00:34:55.511
Wilko loves the smell. but he doesn't
want to cart it around in his pack.

353
00:34:56.595 --> 00:35:01.767
So he slathers it all over his barnet.
goes to sleep.

354
00:35:02.434 --> 00:35:05.062
and in the middle of the night
he wakes up.

355
00:35:05.145 --> 00:35:10.192
and a rat is sitting on his shoulder.
licking the oil off his head.

356
00:35:11.568 --> 00:35:14.113
Wilko panics. and he jumps up.

357
00:35:14.196 --> 00:35:17.658
And when he does. the rat bites
clean through his fucking ear

358
00:35:17.741 --> 00:35:20.077
- and runs off with it!
- No!

359
00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:23.872
He made a hell of a fuss.
yellin'. screamin'.

360
00:35:24.581 --> 00:35:28.002
The best of it was.
he'd put so much bloody oil on himself

361
00:35:28.085 --> 00:35:29.670
that he couldn't wash it off.

362
00:35:29.753 --> 00:35:31.588
He was like a magnet.

363
00:35:31.672 --> 00:35:34.341
Rats left us alone.
but they couldn't get enough of him.

364
00:35:34.425 --> 00:35:35.426
Poor bastard.

365
00:35:43.309 --> 00:35:44.601
Heading back home.

366
00:35:45.728 --> 00:35:47.146
I wonder what they saw.

367
00:35:49.523 --> 00:35:50.774
Watch the ridgelines.

368
00:35:55.946 --> 00:35:57.823
Well. that's your medal sorted. then.

369
00:35:59.158 --> 00:36:00.159
What do you mean?

370
00:36:01.035 --> 00:36:05.581
"Lance Corporal Blake showed unusual valor
rescuing a comrade from certain death."

371
00:36:05.664 --> 00:36:06.915
Blah. blah. blah.

372
00:36:08.584 --> 00:36:09.585
You reckon?

373
00:36:10.669 --> 00:36:11.670
I do.

374
00:36:14.590 --> 00:36:17.384
Well. that'd be nice.
since you lost yours.

375
00:36:18.260 --> 00:36:19.595
I didn't lose mine.

376
00:36:21.096 --> 00:36:22.431
What happened to it. then?

377
00:36:22.890 --> 00:36:24.433
Why do you care?

378
00:36:24.516 --> 00:36:25.768
Why do you not?

379
00:36:27.853 --> 00:36:30.064
I swapped it with a French captain.

380
00:36:30.147 --> 00:36:32.316
Swapped it?

381
00:36:32.399 --> 00:36:33.650
For what?

382
00:36:33.734 --> 00:36:34.818
Bottle of wine.

383
00:36:36.111 --> 00:36:37.821
What did you do that for?

384
00:36:37.905 --> 00:36:39.156
I was thirsty.

385
00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:42.368
What a waste.

386
00:36:44.787 --> 00:36:46.747
You should have
taken it home with you.

387
00:36:46.830 --> 00:36:49.291
You should have given it
to your family.

388
00:36:51.752 --> 00:36:53.170
Men have died for that.

389
00:36:55.047 --> 00:36:56.632
If I got a medal.
I'd take it home.

390
00:36:56.715 --> 00:37:00.219
- Why didn't you just take it home?
- Look. it's just a bit of bloody tin.

391
00:37:00.302 --> 00:37:01.887
It doesn't make you special.

392
00:37:01.970 --> 00:37:03.889
Doesn't make any difference
to anyone.

393
00:37:04.932 --> 00:37:05.933
Yes. it does.

394
00:37:07.184 --> 00:37:08.894
And it's not just a bit of tin.

395
00:37:08.977 --> 00:37:10.104
It's got a ribbon on it.

396
00:37:15.359 --> 00:37:16.860
I hated going home.

397
00:37:17.903 --> 00:37:19.113
I hated it.

398
00:37:21.156 --> 00:37:22.783
When I knew I couldn't stay...

399
00:37:23.951 --> 00:37:26.662
when I knew I had to leave
and they might never see m...

400
00:37:57.985 --> 00:37:58.986
Jesus.

401
00:38:02.364 --> 00:38:03.740
They chopped them all down.

402
00:38:08.036 --> 00:38:09.037
Cherries.

403
00:38:13.208 --> 00:38:14.209
Lamberts.

404
00:38:18.088 --> 00:38:19.298
They might be dukes.

405
00:38:20.132 --> 00:38:22.092
Hard to tell when they aren't in fruit.

406
00:38:22.968 --> 00:38:24.178
What's the difference?

407
00:38:25.429 --> 00:38:27.347
Well. people think there's one type.

408
00:38:28.265 --> 00:38:29.475
But there's lots of them.

409
00:38:29.558 --> 00:38:34.188
Cuthberts. Queen Annes. Montmorencys.
Sweet ones. sour ones.

410
00:38:34.271 --> 00:38:35.939
Why on earth
would you know this?

411
00:38:36.648 --> 00:38:38.233
Mum's got an orchard back home.

412
00:38:39.151 --> 00:38:40.319
Only a few trees.

413
00:38:41.612 --> 00:38:43.947
This time of year.
it looks like it's been snowing.

414
00:38:44.823 --> 00:38:46.033
Blossom everywhere.

415
00:38:47.659 --> 00:38:50.204
And then in May.
we have to pick them.

416
00:38:51.538 --> 00:38:52.539
Me and Joe.

417
00:38:54.416 --> 00:38:55.667
Takes the whole day.

418
00:38:57.044 --> 00:38:58.754
So. these ones all goners?

419
00:38:59.505 --> 00:39:02.674
No. They'll grow again
when the stones rot.

420
00:39:03.509 --> 00:39:05.636
You'll end up with more trees
than before.

421
00:39:11.266 --> 00:39:12.976
It looks abandoned.

422
00:39:13.060 --> 00:39:14.269
Let's hope so.

423
00:39:15.312 --> 00:39:16.647
We have to make sure.

424
00:39:49.763 --> 00:39:51.348
I'll take front. you take back.

425
00:40:34.266 --> 00:40:35.350
Anything?

426
00:40:36.226 --> 00:40:37.227
Nothing.

427
00:40:56.288 --> 00:40:57.706
Did you find any food?

428
00:40:57.789 --> 00:40:58.790
No.

429
00:41:00.417 --> 00:41:01.627
I don't like this place.

430
00:42:09.986 --> 00:42:15.534
Map says get over that ridge
and it's a straight shot to Écoust.

431
00:42:17.119 --> 00:42:18.328
Good.

432
00:43:02.706 --> 00:43:04.040
Is that our friends again?

433
00:43:05.167 --> 00:43:06.376
Looks like it.

434
00:43:07.627 --> 00:43:08.628
Dogfight.

435
00:43:10.338 --> 00:43:12.215
Who's winning?

436
00:43:12.299 --> 00:43:13.341
Us. I think.

437
00:43:14.676 --> 00:43:15.677
Two on one.

438
00:43:19.681 --> 00:43:20.682
They got him.

439
00:44:19.741 --> 00:44:23.453
- We should put him out of his misery.
- No. Get him some water. He needs water.

440
00:44:24.579 --> 00:44:26.623
It's all right. It's all right.

441
00:44:27.541 --> 00:44:29.084
Steady. Stay still.

442
00:44:38.385 --> 00:44:39.970
Stop. Stop!

443
00:44:40.804 --> 00:44:42.681
No. No. no!

444
00:44:48.645 --> 00:44:51.606
You bastard!

445
00:44:51.690 --> 00:44:55.277
You bloody bastard.

446
00:44:57.070 --> 00:44:59.698
Oh. God. no.

447
00:44:59.781 --> 00:45:01.283
Oh. God. no!

448
00:45:02.951 --> 00:45:04.786
Jesus. Jesus. no!

449
00:45:06.079 --> 00:45:08.206
We have to stop the bleeding.

450
00:45:08.290 --> 00:45:09.833
Stop. Stop it! Stop it!

451
00:45:09.916 --> 00:45:11.793
It's all right.
It's going to be all right.

452
00:45:12.794 --> 00:45:13.962
We're going to stand up.

453
00:45:14.045 --> 00:45:16.006
- Okay. yes. Yes.
- Right?

454
00:45:20.552 --> 00:45:23.013
No. I can't. I can't.

455
00:45:24.598 --> 00:45:26.766
- We have to get to an aid post.
- I can't.

456
00:45:26.850 --> 00:45:29.811
- I'll carry you. It isn't very far.
- Just bring a doctor here.

457
00:45:29.895 --> 00:45:31.563
We can't. We have to go together.

458
00:45:33.273 --> 00:45:34.399
We're going to get up.

459
00:45:35.025 --> 00:45:36.234
We're going to get up.

460
00:45:42.449 --> 00:45:44.200
- Stop!
- Come on.

461
00:45:44.284 --> 00:45:45.285
Please stop!

462
00:45:46.077 --> 00:45:49.539
Put me down!
Put me down. you bastard. please!

463
00:45:49.623 --> 00:45:50.624
Put me down!

464
00:46:01.384 --> 00:46:03.136
You have to try to keep moving.

465
00:46:03.219 --> 00:46:04.721
Let's just sit.

466
00:46:04.804 --> 00:46:06.473
- Let me sit.
- No. we can't.

467
00:46:06.556 --> 00:46:08.266
We have to find the 2nd. remember?

468
00:46:08.350 --> 00:46:09.976
Your brother. We have to go now.

469
00:46:10.060 --> 00:46:11.978
You can start on without me.
I'll catch up.

470
00:46:12.062 --> 00:46:13.980
No. You can't stay here.

471
00:46:14.856 --> 00:46:17.108
We have to move. All right?

472
00:46:17.192 --> 00:46:19.486
We have to move. Now. come on.

473
00:46:19.569 --> 00:46:21.613
Come on!

474
00:46:21.696 --> 00:46:23.406
Come on. That's it.

475
00:46:23.490 --> 00:46:26.242
Come on. come on. Come on.

476
00:46:32.082 --> 00:46:34.793
Your brother.
We have to find your brother.

477
00:46:37.837 --> 00:46:38.922
You'll recognize him.

478
00:46:40.924 --> 00:46:42.634
He looks like me.

479
00:46:42.717 --> 00:46:45.345
And he's a bit older.

480
00:46:58.191 --> 00:46:59.192
What are they?

481
00:47:01.987 --> 00:47:03.446
Are we being shelled?

482
00:47:05.073 --> 00:47:07.325
They're embers. The barn is on fire.

483
00:47:12.706 --> 00:47:13.915
I've been hit.

484
00:47:16.001 --> 00:47:17.210
What was it?

485
00:47:18.670 --> 00:47:19.879
You were stabbed.

486
00:47:25.844 --> 00:47:27.429
Am I dying?

487
00:47:36.271 --> 00:47:37.272
Yes.

488
00:47:39.024 --> 00:47:40.275
Yes. I think you are.

489
00:47:57.959 --> 00:48:00.462
- This?
- Inside.

490
00:48:24.486 --> 00:48:26.780
Will you write to my mum for me?

491
00:48:28.281 --> 00:48:29.282
I will.

492
00:48:32.410 --> 00:48:33.870
Tell her I wasn't scared.

493
00:48:38.374 --> 00:48:39.375
Anything else?

494
00:48:42.420 --> 00:48:43.713
I love them.

495
00:48:46.132 --> 00:48:47.133
I wish that...

496
00:48:49.803 --> 00:48:51.054
I wish that...

497
00:48:57.352 --> 00:48:58.561
Talk to me.

498
00:49:01.272 --> 00:49:02.982
Tell me you know the way.

499
00:49:06.569 --> 00:49:07.737
I know the way.

500
00:49:09.531 --> 00:49:12.283
I'm going to head southeast
until I hit Écoust.

501
00:49:13.284 --> 00:49:14.786
I'll pass through the town

502
00:49:14.869 --> 00:49:17.705
and out to the east
all the way to Croisilles Wood.

503
00:49:18.748 --> 00:49:20.375
It'll be dark by then.

504
00:49:21.459 --> 00:49:22.544
That won't bother me.

505
00:49:23.837 --> 00:49:25.630
I'll find the 2nd.

506
00:49:25.713 --> 00:49:27.757
I'll give them the message.

507
00:49:27.841 --> 00:49:30.260
and then I'll find your brother.

508
00:49:30.343 --> 00:49:33.096
Just like you. a little older.

509
00:51:36.469 --> 00:51:37.762
You all right. mate?

510
00:51:38.972 --> 00:51:41.140
Hey. it's all right. It's okay.

511
00:51:42.141 --> 00:51:43.434
Come on. Help him.

512
00:51:52.777 --> 00:51:53.778
Jesus.

513
00:51:54.279 --> 00:51:55.363
What happened to him?

514
00:51:57.198 --> 00:52:00.118
Was it the plane?
We saw the smoke.

515
00:52:00.201 --> 00:52:01.202
Yeah.

516
00:52:18.219 --> 00:52:19.929
Go and fetch his things.

517
00:52:20.013 --> 00:52:21.014
- Sir.
- Sir.

518
00:52:25.226 --> 00:52:26.227
A friend?

519
00:52:29.814 --> 00:52:31.024
What are you doing here?

520
00:52:32.025 --> 00:52:34.569
I have an urgent message
for the 2nd Devons.

521
00:52:34.652 --> 00:52:36.738
Orders to stop
tomorrow morning's attack.

522
00:52:37.363 --> 00:52:39.157
And where are they stationed?

523
00:52:39.240 --> 00:52:40.491
Just beyond Écoust.

524
00:52:41.617 --> 00:52:42.618
Come with me.

525
00:52:49.417 --> 00:52:51.419
Come with me. Corporal.
That's an order.

526
00:52:51.961 --> 00:52:54.630
We're passing through Écoust.
We can take you some of the way.

527
00:52:57.050 --> 00:52:58.051
Sir.

528
00:53:23.326 --> 00:53:24.911
Come on. Sergeant.

529
00:53:24.994 --> 00:53:26.662
Put more men at the base.

530
00:53:27.372 --> 00:53:29.499
At the trunk!
It'll be heavier there.

531
00:53:30.583 --> 00:53:31.793
Might be a tight squeeze.

532
00:53:31.876 --> 00:53:34.462
No. you're not
going to be able to just lift it.

533
00:53:34.545 --> 00:53:36.798
Pivot the front end to the left.

534
00:53:36.881 --> 00:53:39.342
Jesus. they don't
make things easy. do they?

535
00:53:39.425 --> 00:53:43.012
They could at least have retreated
with a bit of grace. Bastards.

536
00:53:43.096 --> 00:53:44.097
Sir.

537
00:53:44.680 --> 00:53:46.599
- You're not one of mine.
- No. sir.

538
00:53:46.682 --> 00:53:49.685
He has an urgent message
to deliver to the 2nd Devons. sir.

539
00:53:49.769 --> 00:53:50.853
Can you get past it?

540
00:53:50.937 --> 00:53:52.438
- No. sir.
- Oh. for God's sake.

541
00:53:52.522 --> 00:53:53.773
Just move it!

542
00:53:54.857 --> 00:53:57.026
There's room in the casuals' truck. sir.

543
00:53:57.568 --> 00:53:59.779
- He has orders.
- Yes. yes. all right.

544
00:53:59.862 --> 00:54:02.407
Come on. now.
You can get through there sideways.

545
00:54:07.203 --> 00:54:08.538
How did you get here. sir?

546
00:54:09.205 --> 00:54:12.083
Crossed no-man's-land
just outside Bapaume.

547
00:54:13.000 --> 00:54:14.210
Took us the whole night.

548
00:54:14.710 --> 00:54:16.796
Bumped into a couple of Hun stragglers
on the way

549
00:54:16.879 --> 00:54:18.589
who made a nuisance of themselves.

550
00:54:19.173 --> 00:54:21.717
- You going up to the new line?
- Attempting to.

551
00:54:22.552 --> 00:54:25.930
The Newfoundlands have pushed forwards
and requested reinforcements.

552
00:54:28.015 --> 00:54:29.559
I'm sorry about your friend.

553
00:54:31.185 --> 00:54:33.980
May I tell you something
that you probably already know?

554
00:54:35.982 --> 00:54:37.692
It doesn't do to dwell on it.

555
00:54:38.943 --> 00:54:40.069
No. sir.

556
00:54:41.112 --> 00:54:44.073
Hop on.

557
00:54:44.157 --> 00:54:45.408
Make some space there.

558
00:54:47.827 --> 00:54:48.953
Come on. In you get!

559
00:55:05.803 --> 00:55:08.222
All right. Here we go again. boys.

560
00:55:11.184 --> 00:55:14.395
Welcome aboard the night bus
to fuck knows where.

561
00:55:18.191 --> 00:55:19.400
Is that a dead dog?

562
00:55:21.402 --> 00:55:23.321
- You got a fag?
- Yeah. There you go.

563
00:55:39.962 --> 00:55:43.216
- Butler. oi. Carry on with that story.
- Yeah.

564
00:55:43.299 --> 00:55:46.135
Right. so. when we get off the train.

565
00:55:46.761 --> 00:55:49.639
Beaufoy comes up to us
and he's having a right go.

566
00:55:50.890 --> 00:55:54.268
"Lance Corporal. whatever one does.
one never lets standards slip."

567
00:55:54.352 --> 00:55:56.312
Then Scott comes out the latrine.

568
00:55:56.395 --> 00:55:58.856
He wipes his hand
on the back of Beaufoy's jacket.

569
00:55:58.940 --> 00:56:01.317
Shit all down his back.

570
00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:05.071
- Was that meant to be Captain Beaufoy?
- Piss off. you. You can't do any better.

571
00:56:05.905 --> 00:56:08.449
"Men. your rifle stocks
are an embarrassment

572
00:56:08.533 --> 00:56:10.409
to the entire expeditionary force!"

573
00:56:10.493 --> 00:56:11.702
- Nah.
- No.

574
00:56:11.786 --> 00:56:13.412
You're both bloody awful.

575
00:56:13.496 --> 00:56:15.915
You don't know.
You barely even speak the bloody language.

576
00:56:15.998 --> 00:56:17.792
He's got a better grasp of it
than you. Cooke.

577
00:56:17.875 --> 00:56:19.252
Go on. Jondalar. Give it a go.

578
00:56:19.335 --> 00:56:21.921
- Let's hear it. Jonny.
- Let's hear it. Go on.

579
00:56:22.380 --> 00:56:26.050
"Rossi!
Never in my 200 years as a soldier

580
00:56:26.133 --> 00:56:28.719
have I seen such a sorry excuse
for a latrine pit!"

581
00:56:28.803 --> 00:56:31.847
Shite. That is total shit.

582
00:56:32.765 --> 00:56:36.519
- Could've taken my teeth out with that.
- You could do with a new set.

583
00:56:41.732 --> 00:56:43.401
You got somewhere
you need to be?

584
00:56:46.153 --> 00:56:48.406
- No.
- Arsehole needs driving lessons.

585
00:57:04.171 --> 00:57:06.007
- He should reverse.
- Yeah.

586
00:57:07.592 --> 00:57:08.759
Try it in reverse.

587
00:57:09.677 --> 00:57:11.262
Reverse!

588
00:57:18.519 --> 00:57:21.022
No. Stop. Stop!

589
00:57:21.105 --> 00:57:22.565
Everyone needs to get out.

590
00:57:23.691 --> 00:57:24.692
All out!

591
00:57:26.527 --> 00:57:28.404
- Come on!
- All right. all right.

592
00:57:28.487 --> 00:57:29.822
Keep your bloody hair on.

593
00:57:30.865 --> 00:57:31.866
Right.

594
00:57:32.491 --> 00:57:35.161
One. two. three!

595
00:57:42.293 --> 00:57:44.170
We need to get some wood.
put it under the wheels.

596
00:57:44.253 --> 00:57:46.714
No. we haven't got the time.
We all need to push.

597
00:57:46.797 --> 00:57:48.424
Come on. Come on!

598
00:57:49.884 --> 00:57:51.552
Come on!

599
00:57:55.431 --> 00:57:58.434
Please! I have to go now. Please.

600
00:58:00.811 --> 00:58:03.064
All right. come on. lads.
Come on.

601
00:58:03.147 --> 00:58:04.315
Come on. boys.

602
00:58:04.398 --> 00:58:06.817
One. two. three.

603
00:58:18.537 --> 00:58:20.581
Come on. boys!
One last push. yeah?

604
00:58:20.665 --> 00:58:22.750
One. two. three!

605
00:58:35.888 --> 00:58:39.266
Back in. Get back in. Go.

606
00:58:40.851 --> 00:58:41.977
Are you all right?

607
00:58:43.229 --> 00:58:46.482
Here. driver. how about you try to keep it
on the bloody road for a change?

608
00:58:46.565 --> 00:58:47.900
Piss off!

609
00:59:07.128 --> 00:59:08.504
So. where are you going?

610
00:59:10.256 --> 00:59:12.758
I have to get to the 2nd Devons.
just past Écoust.

611
00:59:14.093 --> 00:59:15.094
Why?

612
00:59:16.095 --> 00:59:17.888
They're attacking at dawn.

613
00:59:17.972 --> 00:59:19.557
I have orders to stop them.

614
00:59:19.640 --> 00:59:20.683
How come?

615
00:59:22.226 --> 00:59:24.937
- They're walking into a trap.
- How many?

616
00:59:26.063 --> 00:59:28.149
Sixteen hundred.

617
00:59:29.567 --> 00:59:30.568
Jesus.

618
00:59:33.028 --> 00:59:34.739
Why did they send you
on your own?

619
00:59:36.198 --> 00:59:37.199
They didn't.

620
00:59:37.908 --> 00:59:39.326
There were two of us.

621
00:59:40.411 --> 00:59:41.704
So. now it's down to you.

622
00:59:42.747 --> 00:59:43.748
Yes.

623
00:59:45.124 --> 00:59:46.250
You'll never make it.

624
00:59:50.880 --> 00:59:52.047
Yes. I will.

625
00:59:58.888 --> 00:59:59.889
Thank you.

626
01:00:02.767 --> 01:00:03.768
Look at it.

627
01:00:04.727 --> 01:00:05.853
Fucking look at it.

628
01:00:07.438 --> 01:00:09.023
Three years fightin' over this.

629
01:00:10.274 --> 01:00:12.401
We should've just
let the bastards keep it.

630
01:00:13.235 --> 01:00:16.739
- I mean. who machine-guns cows?
- Huns with extra bullets.

631
01:00:17.531 --> 01:00:18.741
Bastards.

632
01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:21.118
Clever.

633
01:00:21.202 --> 01:00:23.245
They know if they don't shoot the cow...

634
01:00:24.288 --> 01:00:25.915
you will eat it.

635
01:00:25.998 --> 01:00:27.249
Still bastards.

636
01:00:27.333 --> 01:00:29.418
Yeah. it's not even
our bloody country.

637
01:00:30.002 --> 01:00:32.463
- How long gone do you reckon they are?
- Why?

638
01:00:33.214 --> 01:00:36.091
- Worried we'll catch up with them?
- Yeah.

639
01:00:36.175 --> 01:00:38.385
Right. Be a bloody miracle at this rate.

640
01:00:38.469 --> 01:00:40.679
Yeah. they're probably
right round the next corner.

641
01:00:40.763 --> 01:00:42.348
Piss off. No. they're not.

642
01:00:43.599 --> 01:00:46.477
Why don't they just
bloody well give up?

643
01:00:47.770 --> 01:00:51.065
- Don't they wanna go home?
- They hate their wives and mothers.

644
01:00:51.148 --> 01:00:54.401
And Germany must be a shithole.

645
01:00:55.236 --> 01:00:56.779
They're retreatin'.

646
01:00:56.862 --> 01:00:58.447
They're miles back.

647
01:00:58.531 --> 01:01:00.115
Got 'em on the ropes. at least.

648
01:01:01.158 --> 01:01:03.911
No. We don't.

649
01:01:06.455 --> 01:01:08.207
Bollocks.
What's up now?

650
01:01:08.290 --> 01:01:11.335
- Not another bloody tree.
- The bridge is down.

651
01:01:11.418 --> 01:01:13.754
That's a shame.

652
01:01:13.838 --> 01:01:15.881
Looks like I'll be getting out here.

653
01:01:15.965 --> 01:01:16.966
Good luck.

654
01:01:17.758 --> 01:01:19.802
Keep some of that luck
for yourself. pal.

655
01:01:19.885 --> 01:01:21.512
- Think you'll be needing it.
- Good luck. mate.

656
01:01:21.595 --> 01:01:24.056
Good luck. guv.
Don't balls it up.

657
01:01:24.974 --> 01:01:26.392
I hope you get there.

658
01:01:27.852 --> 01:01:28.853
Thank you.

659
01:01:32.690 --> 01:01:35.901
The next bridge is six miles.
We'll have to divert.

660
01:01:35.985 --> 01:01:38.445
I can't. sir. I don't have the time.

661
01:01:39.363 --> 01:01:40.531
Of course.

662
01:01:42.491 --> 01:01:43.492
Best of luck.

663
01:01:44.577 --> 01:01:45.578
Thank you. sir.

664
01:01:49.331 --> 01:01:50.332
Corporal?

665
01:01:51.500 --> 01:01:53.794
If you do manage
to get to Colonel Mackenzie...

666
01:01:55.296 --> 01:01:56.839
make sure there are witnesses.

667
01:01:58.257 --> 01:02:00.259
- They are direct orders. sir.
- I know.

668
01:02:02.011 --> 01:02:04.013
But some men just want the fight.

669
01:02:06.765 --> 01:02:07.892
Thank you. sir.

670
01:02:12.521 --> 01:02:15.399
Driver! Move off!

671
01:12:53.703 --> 01:12:55.830
Anglais.

672
01:12:55.914 --> 01:12:57.707
Not German.

673
01:12:57.791 --> 01:12:58.792
Friend.

674
01:12:59.626 --> 01:13:00.835
I'm a friend.

675
01:13:04.214 --> 01:13:06.383
This place. this town...

676
01:13:07.217 --> 01:13:08.218
Écoust?

677
01:13:18.311 --> 01:13:19.312
Others?

678
01:13:19.980 --> 01:13:21.731
No. Just me.

679
01:13:24.484 --> 01:13:25.694
Only me.

680
01:13:28.947 --> 01:13:30.448
I need to be somewhere.

681
01:13:31.866 --> 01:13:34.869
I need to find a wood to the southeast.

682
01:13:36.913 --> 01:13:38.748
Trees.

683
01:13:42.919 --> 01:13:44.129
Croiset?

684
01:13:44.212 --> 01:13:45.380
Croisilles?

685
01:13:45.463 --> 01:13:46.464
Yes.

686
01:13:50.594 --> 01:13:51.928
River.

687
01:13:52.012 --> 01:13:55.056
River. It go there.

688
01:13:55.974 --> 01:13:57.976
Trees. Croisilles.

689
01:15:30.944 --> 01:15:31.945
Thank you.

690
01:15:59.723 --> 01:16:01.057
A girl?

691
01:16:19.451 --> 01:16:20.660
What is her name?

692
01:16:25.623 --> 01:16:27.000
Who is her mother?

693
01:16:36.050 --> 01:16:37.218
I have food.

694
01:16:39.012 --> 01:16:40.013
Here.

695
01:16:43.600 --> 01:16:44.601
I have these.

696
01:16:46.352 --> 01:16:49.439
But you can have them.
Here. take them all.

697
01:16:49.522 --> 01:16:51.566
For you and the child. Here.

698
01:17:02.702 --> 01:17:03.912
Milk?

699
01:17:24.390 --> 01:17:25.517
Merci.

700
01:17:33.900 --> 01:17:35.151
Bonjour.

701
01:17:37.237 --> 01:17:39.113
Bonjour.

702
01:17:42.742 --> 01:17:44.744
Children? You?

703
01:17:48.164 --> 01:17:49.332
It's all right.

704
01:17:56.506 --> 01:17:58.216
Continuez.

705
01:18:04.138 --> 01:18:06.266
"They went to sea in a Sieve. they did...

706
01:18:07.642 --> 01:18:09.769
In a Sieve they went to sea:

707
01:18:11.187 --> 01:18:13.648
In spite of all their friends could say...

708
01:18:14.691 --> 01:18:17.360
On a winter's morn. on a stormy day.

709
01:18:18.319 --> 01:18:20.405
In a Sieve they went to sea!

710
01:18:21.656 --> 01:18:24.701
Far and few. far and few.

711
01:18:24.784 --> 01:18:27.120
Are the lands where the Jumblies live;

712
01:18:28.746 --> 01:18:32.333
Their heads are green.
and their hands are blue...

713
01:18:34.919 --> 01:18:37.171
And they went to sea in a Sieve."

714
01:19:24.552 --> 01:19:28.097
Stay. Stay. Please.

715
01:19:28.181 --> 01:19:29.390
I have to go.

716
01:19:39.067 --> 01:19:40.360
Please.

717
01:19:40.443 --> 01:19:41.444
I'm sorry.

718
01:21:50.990 --> 01:21:52.200
Baumer?

719
01:21:56.079 --> 01:21:57.246
Baumer?

720
01:21:59.499 --> 01:22:01.667
Baumer.

721
01:22:06.422 --> 01:22:07.507
Baumer!

722
01:32:25.999 --> 01:32:28.502
D Company. move out!

723
01:32:28.585 --> 01:32:29.670
You all right. pal?

724
01:32:31.046 --> 01:32:32.214
Where you from?

725
01:32:32.297 --> 01:32:34.633
- He's probably got the wind up.
- He's not one of ours.

726
01:32:34.717 --> 01:32:35.968
He's bloody soaked.

727
01:32:36.635 --> 01:32:38.929
Fuck it. Let's just pick him up
and take him with us.

728
01:32:39.012 --> 01:32:40.848
Have to find the Devons.

729
01:32:42.015 --> 01:32:43.016
What's he saying?

730
01:32:43.100 --> 01:32:44.727
What's that. mate?

731
01:32:44.810 --> 01:32:46.019
The Devons.

732
01:32:46.979 --> 01:32:48.981
I have to find the Devons.

733
01:32:50.399 --> 01:32:51.483
We're the Devons.

734
01:32:55.821 --> 01:32:56.989
You're the Devons?

735
01:32:57.072 --> 01:32:58.073
Yes. Corp.

736
01:33:00.200 --> 01:33:01.744
Why haven't you gone over?

737
01:33:01.827 --> 01:33:04.955
- We're the second wave.
- They don't send us all at once.

738
01:33:05.038 --> 01:33:06.582
Yeah. we're D Company.

739
01:33:06.665 --> 01:33:09.251
We spent the night diggin' in.
We go last.

740
01:33:11.545 --> 01:33:13.088
Are you all right?

741
01:33:13.172 --> 01:33:14.381
Mackenzie.

742
01:33:14.465 --> 01:33:15.674
Where's Colonel Mackenzie?

743
01:33:15.758 --> 01:33:17.176
Well. he's down at the line.

744
01:33:17.885 --> 01:33:19.052
- Which way?
- This way.

745
01:33:19.136 --> 01:33:20.471
We're headed up there now.

746
01:33:21.263 --> 01:33:23.265
Steady on. mate.
Where you going?

747
01:33:44.661 --> 01:33:45.662
Move!

748
01:33:49.958 --> 01:33:51.043
Let me by!

749
01:33:55.547 --> 01:33:56.715
Let me through!

750
01:33:56.799 --> 01:34:00.093
Remember. follow your platoon commander.

751
01:34:00.803 --> 01:34:03.806
Stay spread out
and watch for his orders.

752
01:34:03.889 --> 01:34:06.892
- Where is your commanding officer?
- He's in the holding pen.

753
01:34:06.975 --> 01:34:10.854
Raise your signal flags
or fire the signal flares

754
01:34:10.938 --> 01:34:13.482
when you've taken your section
of the Hun line.

755
01:34:13.565 --> 01:34:16.527
B Company. stand to.
Now listen and listen well.

756
01:34:16.610 --> 01:34:18.612
On the first mark.
A Company will advance.

757
01:34:18.695 --> 01:34:20.823
B Company will then move
to the front line.

758
01:34:20.906 --> 01:34:23.116
Sir. I have a message
from General Erinmore.

759
01:34:23.200 --> 01:34:25.661
- Who the fuck are you?
- The attack has been called off.

760
01:34:25.744 --> 01:34:27.621
General Erinmore
has called off the attack.

761
01:34:27.704 --> 01:34:30.707
Balls. man. We're about to go over.
We've got them on the run!

762
01:34:30.791 --> 01:34:32.543
You don't.
Please don't send your men over.

763
01:34:32.626 --> 01:34:33.585
Get out of the way!

764
01:34:33.669 --> 01:34:36.713
These are direct orders from army command!
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?

765
01:34:36.797 --> 01:34:39.508
Jesus Christ. man!
Go and see the captain!

766
01:34:39.591 --> 01:34:41.844
Now. I want us up there quickly.
you understand?

767
01:34:41.927 --> 01:34:44.555
- Do you understand?
- Yes. sir!

768
01:34:45.681 --> 01:34:48.392
NCOs collect flares and signal flags.
Keep to your stations.

769
01:34:48.475 --> 01:34:49.893
Oi. Oi!

770
01:34:58.402 --> 01:35:00.946
Nine and ten section at the ready!

771
01:35:01.697 --> 01:35:04.950
We will advance
on the first whistle blast!

772
01:35:07.327 --> 01:35:09.538
The man next to you falls. keep moving.

773
01:35:09.621 --> 01:35:11.790
Your orders are to break the lines.

774
01:35:11.874 --> 01:35:14.209
- Where is the captain?
- He's over there.

775
01:35:16.587 --> 01:35:18.589
Sir! Sir!

776
01:35:20.090 --> 01:35:22.342
Captain. I have a message.

777
01:35:22.426 --> 01:35:23.844
This attack is called off.

778
01:35:23.927 --> 01:35:26.263
You have to stop.
You have to stop.

779
01:35:30.183 --> 01:35:31.643
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?

780
01:35:32.269 --> 01:35:34.438
Where is Mackenzie?

781
01:36:04.343 --> 01:36:06.470
Back! Hold fast!

782
01:36:08.931 --> 01:36:12.100
Sir. I have orders to stop this attack!

783
01:36:12.184 --> 01:36:13.185
What?

784
01:36:13.268 --> 01:36:15.604
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?

785
01:36:15.687 --> 01:36:17.397
He's further up the line.

786
01:36:17.481 --> 01:36:18.398
How far?

787
01:36:18.482 --> 01:36:21.026
Three hundred yards.
He's in a cut-and-cover.

788
01:36:21.109 --> 01:36:23.820
You'll have to wait
until the first wave goes over.

789
01:36:23.904 --> 01:36:25.864
No. No. I can't.

790
01:36:33.622 --> 01:36:37.042
Seven platoon. 30 seconds!

791
01:36:48.762 --> 01:36:52.057
You can't possibly make it that way. man!
Are you bloody insane?

792
01:36:56.687 --> 01:36:58.855
What the hell are you doing.
Lance Corporal?

793
01:36:59.314 --> 01:37:01.066
No! No. no. no. no!

794
01:38:05.881 --> 01:38:07.382
Get ready!

795
01:38:07.466 --> 01:38:09.634
- Colonel Mackenzie!
- He's in there.

796
01:38:11.386 --> 01:38:12.471
Two minutes!

797
01:38:12.971 --> 01:38:13.972
Let me through!

798
01:38:14.056 --> 01:38:15.724
Hey! Hey!

799
01:38:15.807 --> 01:38:18.643
Let me through! I have to get through!

800
01:38:18.727 --> 01:38:19.936
I have to see Colonel Mackenzie!

801
01:38:20.020 --> 01:38:21.688
- What are you doing?
- I have to stop this attack!

802
01:38:21.772 --> 01:38:22.939
Colonel. we've seen flares.

803
01:38:23.023 --> 01:38:25.150
Men on the left flank
have made it to the German line.

804
01:38:25.233 --> 01:38:27.527
- Colonel! Colonel!
- Hold him! Hold him!

805
01:38:27.611 --> 01:38:29.863
Listen to me.
Listen to me. I have a letter.

806
01:38:29.946 --> 01:38:31.531
I need to see Colonel Mackenzie.

807
01:38:31.615 --> 01:38:33.241
There's no bloody way
you're gettin' in there!

808
01:38:33.325 --> 01:38:34.951
Sergeant. send the next wave!

809
01:38:35.035 --> 01:38:36.161
No!

810
01:38:36.244 --> 01:38:38.288
Second wave. prepare yourselves!

811
01:38:38.371 --> 01:38:40.290
- Colonel Mackenzie!
- Concentrate everything there.

812
01:38:40.373 --> 01:38:42.626
This attack is not to go ahead!

813
01:38:42.709 --> 01:38:45.420
You have been ordered to stop!
You have to stop!

814
01:38:45.504 --> 01:38:46.838
Who the hell are you?

815
01:38:47.380 --> 01:38:49.716
Lance Corporal Schofield. sir. 8th.

816
01:38:49.800 --> 01:38:52.552
I have orders from General Erinmore
to call off this attack.

817
01:38:52.636 --> 01:38:54.054
You're too late. Lance Corporal.

818
01:38:54.137 --> 01:38:57.641
Sir. these orders are from army command.
You have to read them.

819
01:38:57.724 --> 01:39:00.727
- Shall we hold back the second wave. sir?
- No. Major. Hesitate now and we lose.

820
01:39:00.811 --> 01:39:03.021
- Victory's only 500 yards away.
- Sir!

821
01:39:03.105 --> 01:39:04.272
Please. read the letter.

822
01:39:04.356 --> 01:39:07.317
I have heard it all before.

823
01:39:07.400 --> 01:39:09.486
I'm not gonna wait until dusk or for fog.

824
01:39:09.569 --> 01:39:12.322
I'm not calling back my men only
to send them out there again tomorrow.

825
01:39:12.405 --> 01:39:13.907
not when we've got the bastards
on the run.

826
01:39:13.990 --> 01:39:16.618
- This is their last stand.
- The Germans planned this. sir.

827
01:39:18.036 --> 01:39:21.373
They've been planning it for months.
They want you to attack.

828
01:39:22.582 --> 01:39:23.834
Read the letter.

829
01:39:44.563 --> 01:39:46.189
- Major?
- Yes. sir?

830
01:39:48.775 --> 01:39:49.985
Stand them down.

831
01:39:50.777 --> 01:39:52.237
- Yes. sir.
- Call up the orderlies.

832
01:39:52.320 --> 01:39:53.655
Tend the wounded.

833
01:39:53.738 --> 01:39:55.323
Hold the line
in case they counter.

834
01:39:55.407 --> 01:39:56.908
Yes. sir!

835
01:39:56.992 --> 01:39:59.411
Stand down! Stand down!

836
01:40:02.539 --> 01:40:05.750
Stand down!

837
01:40:05.834 --> 01:40:09.087
- Cease fire! Cease fire!
- Stand down!

838
01:40:13.049 --> 01:40:15.427
I hoped today
might be a good day.

839
01:40:17.762 --> 01:40:20.098
Hope is a dangerous thing.

840
01:40:22.225 --> 01:40:25.562
That's it for now. and then next week
command will send a different message.

841
01:40:26.563 --> 01:40:27.814
"Attack at dawn."

842
01:40:31.735 --> 01:40:33.737
There is only one way this war ends.

843
01:40:36.281 --> 01:40:38.074
Last man standing.

844
01:40:43.788 --> 01:40:45.415
Have someone see to your wounds.

845
01:40:48.501 --> 01:40:50.587
Now. fuck off. Lance Corporal.

846
01:40:56.468 --> 01:40:59.763
Bearers! Stretcher bearers!

847
01:41:00.805 --> 01:41:03.934
Bearers! Stretcher bearers!

848
01:41:04.601 --> 01:41:05.810
Well done. lad.

849
01:41:07.020 --> 01:41:08.146
Thank you. sir.

850
01:41:10.607 --> 01:41:12.525
Do you know where
Lieutenant Blake is. sir?

851
01:41:13.068 --> 01:41:14.611
Blake?

852
01:41:14.694 --> 01:41:16.529
There were two of us.

853
01:41:16.613 --> 01:41:18.865
I was sent here with his brother.

854
01:41:21.159 --> 01:41:24.704
Well. knowing Lieutenant Blake.
he would have gone over with his men.

855
01:41:24.788 --> 01:41:26.331
He was in the first wave.

856
01:41:27.958 --> 01:41:29.834
How could I find him. sir?

857
01:41:29.918 --> 01:41:33.171
You can try the casualty clearing station
behind the line.

858
01:41:34.798 --> 01:41:36.007
Otherwise...

859
01:41:39.469 --> 01:41:40.637
Thank you. sir.

860
01:41:41.513 --> 01:41:42.847
Major Hepburn. sir!

861
01:42:34.274 --> 01:42:37.277
Just keep movin'.
Keep movin'. keep movin'.

862
01:43:02.427 --> 01:43:05.764
Sergeant. I have to find Lieutenant Blake.
Do you know where he is?

863
01:43:05.847 --> 01:43:06.848
No.

864
01:43:27.035 --> 01:43:28.161
Clear the way.

865
01:43:28.745 --> 01:43:32.207
- Sir. is Lieutenant Blake here?
- No idea.

866
01:43:33.666 --> 01:43:34.834
Move along. Corporal.

867
01:43:36.419 --> 01:43:38.505
If you can walk. move to the triage area.

868
01:43:40.673 --> 01:43:43.635
Help me!

869
01:43:46.388 --> 01:43:47.514
Lieutenant Blake!

870
01:43:51.017 --> 01:43:54.354
Sir. he's out.

871
01:43:56.981 --> 01:43:58.525
Out of the bloody way!

872
01:43:59.901 --> 01:44:01.152
Blake?

873
01:44:03.780 --> 01:44:05.865
Has anyone seen Lieutenant Blake?

874
01:44:07.742 --> 01:44:10.703
He's hemorrhaging.
Go quickly. He needs a surgeon.

875
01:44:17.502 --> 01:44:19.546
Amputation. Straight to surgery.

876
01:44:24.384 --> 01:44:25.552
My leg!

877
01:44:28.680 --> 01:44:30.390
I need some help here! Quickly!

878
01:44:35.228 --> 01:44:37.313
I need something now!

879
01:44:41.151 --> 01:44:42.569
Coming through!

880
01:44:56.458 --> 01:44:58.293
All right. come on. boys.

881
01:44:58.376 --> 01:45:01.296
He's taken one in the leg.
He's lost a lot of blood.

882
01:45:01.379 --> 01:45:02.297
Sir.

883
01:45:02.380 --> 01:45:04.466
- Lieutenant Blake?
- Yes?

884
01:45:06.342 --> 01:45:07.927
Do you need medical assistance?

885
01:45:09.512 --> 01:45:12.515
No. sir. I'm from the 8th.

886
01:45:12.599 --> 01:45:14.267
What the hell are you doing here?

887
01:45:15.226 --> 01:45:18.104
- I was sent here to deliver a message.
- The 8th?

888
01:45:18.188 --> 01:45:19.564
You must know my brother.

889
01:45:20.899 --> 01:45:23.902
- I was sent here with him.
- Tom's here? Where is he?

890
01:45:30.575 --> 01:45:31.951
It was very quick.

891
01:45:34.579 --> 01:45:35.788
I'm sorry.

892
01:45:59.938 --> 01:46:01.105
What's your name?

893
01:46:02.273 --> 01:46:03.399
Schofield. sir.

894
01:46:06.861 --> 01:46:08.112
Sorry. what?

895
01:46:08.905 --> 01:46:10.698
It's Schofield. sir.

896
01:46:10.782 --> 01:46:11.991
William Schofield.

897
01:46:13.368 --> 01:46:14.452
Will.

898
01:46:16.871 --> 01:46:19.999
Well. you need some food.
Get yourself to the mess tent.

899
01:46:35.014 --> 01:46:36.015
If I may...

900
01:46:37.100 --> 01:46:38.768
I'd like to write to your mother.

901
01:46:39.852 --> 01:46:41.854
Tell her that Tom wasn't alone.

902
01:46:45.400 --> 01:46:46.401
Of course.

903
01:46:49.237 --> 01:46:50.238
He was...

904
01:46:52.198 --> 01:46:53.533
He was a good man.

905
01:46:55.743 --> 01:46:57.328
Always telling funny stories.

906
01:47:00.498 --> 01:47:01.833
He saved my life.

907
01:47:06.004 --> 01:47:08.006
I am glad you were with him.

908
01:47:14.262 --> 01:47:15.388
Thank you. Will.

908
01:47:16.305 --> 01:48:16.445
Do you want subtitles for any video?
